  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "aim_wait_fire_mapping",
  "label": "The phrase 'aim. wait. fire.' is mapped onto the man's action of aiming a firearm.",
  "description": "The textual phrase 'aim. wait. fire.' serves as a direct instruction that is visually embodied by the man holding and aiming a handgun. The visual material (the man aiming) is mapped onto the textual instruction, creating an analogical mapping where the man's action represents the literal execution of the steps described in the text. This mapping is reinforced by the man's intense, focused expression and the tactical combat setting, which align with the metaphorical meaning of the phrase — preparation, patience, and decisive action. The mapping is explicit through the juxtaposition of the text and the visual action, where the man becomes the visual instantiation of the textual command.",
